# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Commit policy (see AGENTS.md "Licensing & Commit Policy" and LICENSE):
# This repo is Apache-2.0 and must NOT redistribute copyrighted game assets or
# GPL/AGPL-incompatible tool builds. Only our own authored source, docs, scripts,
# and curated analysis notes are committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Copyrighted game binaries/data — never committed. Users supply their own copy.
original/
references/

# references/ultima3/ is a third-party clone (MIT code, Lairware art/sound),
# added by the owner on 2026-10-24 as a reference implementation only. It is
# covered by the `references/` rule above, but it is NOT part of the pristine
# game backup and must not be treated as one — see docs/external-ultima3-remake.md.
# Listed here so a future gitignore tidy-up cannot accidentally un-ignore it.
references/ultima3/

# Raw runtime dumps of the copyrighted binary (regenerable, derived, bulky).
# The top-level patterns predate tools/spice86_stop.sh, which harvests into one
# subdirectory per labelled run (captures/spice86/<label>/); those subdirs were
# NOT covered, so a harvest would have staged copyrighted derived dumps into
# git. The directory is ignored wholesale now; curated analysis derived from it
# lives in disasm/ and docs/, which stay tracked.
captures/spice86/
captures/spice86/*.bin
captures/spice86/*.json

# Full decompiler dumps — bulky derivative working output; regenerate locally.
# (Curated analysis in disasm/*.md|tsv|txt IS committed.)
decompiled/

# Vendored third-party tool builds — GPL / re-fetchable, not our source.
# GPL build, never committed. The glob also covers dated backups kept when a
# vendored build is replaced (e.g. spice86.pre-b64fix-20261021), so a stray
# `git add -A` cannot pull 160 MB of GPL binaries into the repo. Trailing slash
# means directories only, so tools/spice86_start.sh and friends stay tracked.
tools/spice86*/
tools/reko/
# CiderPress2 cp2 CLI (GPL-3.0, .NET) — vendored image reader for the Apple II
# reference disks, same category as the two above: re-fetchable tool build, not
# our source.  See docs/apple2-reference.md for how it is used.
tools/ciderpress2/

# Scratch run directories (timestamped Spice86 gameplay runs, captures).
tmp/

# Ctrl-S output. The player binary writes screenshots next to its own working
# directory, so a run from the repo root would otherwise leave them committable.
/screenshots/

# Build output.
build/

# OS / editor noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Owner-supplied screenshots of the running game (evidence for on-screen geometry).
# The image is derived from copyrighted game art, so the file stays out of git and
# only the measurements we derive from it are committed, in docs/. See
# docs/phase4-implementation.md § CP4 "Evidence gap".
captures/screenshots/

# User-authorized external raw runtime captures (see captures/external-20261019/PROVENANCE.md).
# Raw dumps stay out of git per the licensing policy; the provenance note is committed.
captures/external-20261019/**/*.json

# Full linear asm dumps are bulky derived artefacts of the copyrighted
# binary (regenerable via tools/extract_asm.py); keep out of git like decompiled/.
disasm/*.asm

# per-function asm slices (regenerable via tools/make_slices.py)
disasm/functions/

# vendored jwasm build (Open Watcom Public License, re-fetchable; see tools/jwasm/README.md)
tools/jwasm/*
!tools/jwasm/README.md

# local secrets (gh token etc.) — never commit
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 4 engine.
# engine/build/ is build output and never committed. The one generated file the
# repo DOES carry is engine/content/gen_content.h: the game's strings, extracted
# from the owner's copy by engine/tools/extract/extractor.py and verified against
# asm/ by `make -C engine content-check`. AGENTS.md § 0 ("The text/art line") is
# the ruling, and the reason it is committed rather than rebuilt is that the asm
# fallback cannot resolve 38 of them and a silent fallback would blank the
# character-creation screen.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
engine/build/
engine/u2
engine/u2-sdl

# Player saves. The engine writes a byte-compatible PLAYER file into
# --save-dir (default ./saves). That is user data, never a repo artefact.
engine/saves/

# Tile cache. Derived from the player's own executable on first run, stamped
# with its SHA-256, and rebuilt when that digest changes. Game content by
# construction, so it never belongs in the repo wherever --save-dir points.
*.u2tl
engine/tests/*.out

# Raw output of the selfmod runtime-capture scans (scratch; the curated note
# disasm/selfmod-capture.md is what is committed).
disasm/selfmod-raw/

# Python bytecode caches from the tools/ scripts. The previous pattern here was
# `pycache`, which matches nothing: gitignore is not a substring match, so the
# directory is named `__pycache__` and needed the underscores.
__pycache__/

.playwright-mcp/

# engine/build-sdl/ is the SDL build tree: compiler output and dep files, same
# rationale as engine/build/ above. It was missed when the sdl target was added, so
# 64 .o files were being tracked and showed as modified on every `make sdl`.
engine/build-sdl/

# Third-party creature data pulled by tools/bestiary_fetch.py: copyrighted rips of
# game art in seven platform variants, the FM Towns frame strips split from them,
# and view.html, which embeds all of it as data URIs. All regenerable. Only our own
# derived table (bestiary/bestiary.tsv) and the prose beside it are committed, per
# the licensing policy above. This is also original art in bulk, so it is forbidden
# to anyone drawing substitute art — see docs/tile-art-spec.md § 2.
bestiary/cache/
bestiary/view.html

# themes/ is built by tools/build_themes.py out of the player's own media
# (references/u2upgrade, original/updated, references/fmtowns). It holds
# extracted game art, so it is never committed - same posture as original/,
# references/, tmp/tiles and bestiary/cache/. See docs/handoff-themes-builder.md.
/themes/
# deploy/novnc/u2-sdl is a COPY of the host build (make -C engine sdl), staged here so the
# image can COPY it. Never commit it: it is build output, and the host binary is the
# one make test actually verified.
deploy/novnc/u2-sdl

# Accidental output directories, and the reason they are ignored rather than just
# deleted. A tool that takes its output path as a positional argument will create a
# directory named after whatever you meant as a help flag: `cp7_dungeon_seed.py -h`
# made `-h/`, and a capture run given `0` made `0/`. Twenty-four PNGs under `0/` were
# committed before anyone looked, and were removed on 2026-11-02. Note that `-h` is
# also a git option, so `git ls-files -h` answers a question you did not ask instead
# of the one you meant — check such names with `git ls-files -- './-h'`.
/-h/
/0/
engine/u2-sdl.exe
engine/build-win/
engine/u2-sdl-static
engine/build-sdlstatic/
